From 70435e4ea95211f79fcb46b166bba80d638c4ecb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FVOCI <150913557+fvoci@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:34:54 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(web): treat a task's schedule as one unit and show exact
 values when asking (D-94 review)

The review of the D-94 first pass found that start_date, due_date and
milestone were merged field by field, so "save mine again" could save a
schedule nobody chose or saw (the server's start 10-05 with my due 10-03
was rejected with 400; the server's 10-05~10-15 with my start 10-03 was
shown and saved as 10-03~10-15), and the confirmation could show a start
date that was then dropped because the merged milestone was on.

- Schedule unit: implementation interpretation of D-94 for tasks. D-94
  asks to handle an event's date, time, time zone and all-day flag as one
  bundle; a task's schedule {start_date, due_date, milestone} is treated
  the same way. Untouched -> the server's whole schedule; changed only by
  me (or to the same value) -> my whole schedule; changed differently on
  both sides -> one clash row with both whole schedules ("start X, due Y"
  or "milestone, due Y"). refresh() shares mergeForm, so it cannot mix
  schedules either. currentInput() and the merge use the same scheduleOf,
  and overwrite() saves the merge it showed, so the row shown is exactly
  what is sent (a test compares the row with the request payload).
- Assignees are compared as a set (the UI appends, the server returns
  them sorted by name), so the same people in another order no longer
  ask or make refresh() save at the old version for a needless 409.
  Tags: validate_tags in tasks.rs trims and drops duplicates but keeps
  the given order and the row is read back as stored, so tag order is
  meaningful and stays compared in order.
- The confirmation shows full values, with line breaks and spaces kept
  (pre-wrap, scrolling inside a max height), each labelled as the server
  value or mine; no more cutting at 80 characters or collapsing spaces.
  Title and description are shown as the server stores them (trimmed),
  and a value of mine that differs from the server's only by surrounding
  spaces is not a clash, so two values that look identical are never
  asked about. Whether I edited a field still compares the raw text, so a
  refresh keeps text being typed with a trailing space.
- Focus: when a save approved in the follower shift preview (after an
  overwrite, a no-clash save, or a first save) answers 409, focus returns
  to "save mine again" instead of falling to the body.
- While the confirmation is open everything in the task detail except the
  conflict notice (and the confirmation in it) is inert, so checklist,
  recurrence, predecessor and parent changes cannot silently close it.
- Order of the rows follows the real form: title, status, priority,
  schedule (start/due; the milestone checkbox belongs to it), description,
  estimate, tags, assignees.
- Escape cancels the confirmation (nothing sent, input kept, focus back to
  "save mine again") and does not reach the surrounding dialog; the
  handler sits on the element itself. No aria-modal: the confirmation is
  inline in the conflict notice, whose other button and the dialog's close
  stay usable, and aria-modal=true would hide them from screen readers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
